A||N||8||kornholio||smaller width tires||||1
Z||000000||kornholio||10-03-1999||04:37 PM||||Is anyone using a set of smaller width tires for their 2m6? The sticker on the door says 215/60/14. I've been thinking of getting thinner tires to help with the wet traction. I'm not too worried about the speedo.  According to this site, (http://www.cs.fredonia.edu/~stei0302/WWW/DAKOTA/TIRECALC/tirecalc.html) I just need to get the right specs for my tires so that my speedo stays accurate enough.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||10-03-1999||07:25 PM||||My 87 SE had 205-70-14 tires all around when I first bought it. This tire size is about the same height as 215-60-14, but are narrower. I've even seen 195-70-14 tires on a couple of Fieros before. Should be no problem going to a smaller size.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87FieroGT||10-04-1999||01:32 AM||||I don't meen to complain, but why would you want to put smaller tires on the Fiero. I would rather have larger tires. In fact, I am getting to put some brand new Konig Rush 16" rims with some 245/45/ZR16's all the way around. The guy at Discount Tire was kind enough to do the math and these size tires are the same diameter as the original 205/60/15's that were on the GT. Just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||10-04-1999||01:58 AM||||Wider tires will hydroplane easier on wet roads, I know from experience. Personally, I like wider tires too, except in the rain, but to each their own.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||10-04-1999||09:32 AM||||My 88 Coupe has the 14x6 factory alloys and came with 195/70R14 tires from the factory.  I put 215/60R14's on it when the 195's wore out.<P>The 215's are much better in the dry and about the same in the wet, but where I really notice a difference is in the snow.  The 215's are awful - they ride over the snow like snowshoes.  The 195's would sink in and get better traction.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||10-04-1999||04:39 PM||||My car hydroplanes in rain, so it'll be hell in snow (yes, I plan on driving it in the winter).  I just need more traction in wet weather and I don't want to get just a wet weather tire like the Aquatreds.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||10-04-1999||07:59 PM||||Got to recomend the Blizzak's,they stick pretty good on glare ice even,last about 3-4 years,and Firestone will dismount everything up to 5 years for free,if you don't have extra wheels.<BR>My '86 S/E V6,5spd came with 195/70 tires.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GT||10-04-1999||08:02 PM||||I have aquatreads on my car and they dont do a darn bit of good.  I really hate driving my car in the wet weather.  This morning, I had to slow down to 30 on a curve near my house which I normally can go around at 55-60 mph. So in short, the aquas dont do much.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||10-06-1999||09:33 AM||||Speaking of tire size.  I have an 86 GT that came with 205/60/15 on the front and 215/60/15's on the back.  That's what it says in my owners manual also.  Just throwing out some more data for those brain cells to juggle.||||reg||1
